/* ---- COMPILES OFF THE MAIN THREAD (2026-10-09, docs/47 "Run 171") ---------------------------------------------------------
 * Run 170: the first-ever compile of a program freezes play -- 0.5-1.2 s for most, 7.8 / 8.8 / 8.7 s for the 6-light vertex
 * programs. SceShaccCg runs on the caller's thread and the Vita has cores to spare, so a WORKER thread compiles the Cg
 * source; the main thread keeps drawing (a list whose pair is not ready goes by the CPU path, a primitive whose fragment
 * program is not ready is not drawn until it is) and picks the result up at the next present.
 *
 * vitaGL is not asked to do anything new: the link wraps shark_compile_shader_extended / shark_clear_output (--wrap in
 * build_game_vita.sh). The worker runs the REAL compile and leaves its output LIVE; at the next present the main thread
 * calls glCompileShader on the same source, the wrapper hands vitaGL that live output (so vitaGL's own walk of the compile
 * output -- matrix parameters, uniform blocks -- sees the right one), and vitaGL's shark_clear_output releases the compiler.
 * One result at a time: the compiler (g_asc_sem) is held from the start of a compile until its output is cleared.
 * A main-thread compile that is NOT a pickup (vitaGL's fixed-function shaders, or async off) takes the compiler the same
 * way: it waits for a compile in flight, and throws away a finished one that has not been picked up (it is re-queued).
